            <ArticleTitle>The art of presenting - Failures, fonts and the future.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>107-108</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1080/0142159X.2016.1231918</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Many of you, like me, will have given countless presentations throughout your career and to wide and varied audiences. I too, like many of you, have never been formally taught how to present, if that is such a thing. So, I got to thinking: in any case, who are &quot;expert presenter&quot; teachers? Some people have it and some people do not - right? In this short piece, I explore what it is to present, how this evolves, and try to pin down the why rather than the how and give you a little insight into my haphazard journey along this process.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
